adjudication.rationale:
The handler’s secret check compares the incoming header value to `process.env.CALCOM_WEBHOOK_SECRET`:

```ts
if (req.headers[process.env.CALCOM_WEBHOOK_HEADER_NAME || "calcom-webhook-secret"] !==
    process.env.CALCOM_WEBHOOK_SECRET) {
  return res.status(403)
}
```

If `CALCOM_WEBHOOK_SECRET` is unset, it evaluates to `undefined`. For a request that also omits the header, `req.headers[...]` is typically `undefined` as well, making the comparison `undefined !== undefined` false, so the request is accepted. That’s an authentication bypass when the secret env var is not configured (assuming `APP_CREDENTIAL_SHARING_ENABLED` is true).
